@jason25417/dsh-session-auto-rename README · What you get：- **Auto-rename** — a new row in a Session's「…」menu, right under Rename. It reads the Session log, weights each user message by recency (τ = 3 days, so the newest turns dominate the topic), asks the default model for a short title, and applies it through the shipped rename RPC. While it runs, a status line at the bottom of the frame reports progress; failures show the reason.
- **Right-click menu** — right-clicking any Session row opens that row's own「…」menu at the pointer. The menu content is the shipped one (pin / rename / auto-rename / fork / archive / copy id), not a re-implementation.
- **Agent tool** — `session_auto_rename({ sessionId })`, the same operation, callable by the model.

@jason25417/dsh-session-auto-rename README · Known limitations：- Right-click reuses the shipped menu by synthesizing the「…」button's click and keeping the portal menu pinned at the pointer. It relies on the sidebar row attributes `data-row-key="session:<id>"` and `span[class*="rowActions"]`; if a DSH release changes that markup, right-click degrades silently while the menu row keeps working.
- The title call goes through `ctx.llm.stream` with the current default model. Switching the composer model changes the route the plugin uses.
- The menu surface re-derives its anchor every frame; the plugin keeps it at the pointer with a transform, so scrolling moves the menu with the anchor instead of leaving it at the original point.
